\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.\cf0  God, who made the earth,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 The air, the sky, the sea,
\par Who gave the light its birth,
\par Careth for me.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  2.  God, who made the grass,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0  The flower, the fruit, the tree,
\par  The day and night to pass,
\par \pard       Careth for me.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\ulnone\b0 
\par  \cf0 3.  God, who made the sun,
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0   The moon, the stars, is He
\par Who, when life's clouds come on,
\par Careth for me.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  4. God who made all things,
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0 On earth, in air, in sea,
\par Who changing seasons brings,
\par Careth for me.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  5. God, who sent His Son
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 To die on Calvary,
\par He, if I lean on Him,
\par  Will care for me.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  6.  When in heaven's bright land,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 I all His loved ones see,
\par I'll sing with that blest band,
\par \pard     'God Cared for me' \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

